  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Dry weather expected this weekend with cool\novernights and warm afternoons. \n\nClouds are gradually clearing and will continue to do so into \nthe overnight hours. Still seeing patches of lingering cloud\ncover but overall trend is for clearing. The evening RNK\nsounding showed a dramatic drop in moisture just above the\nsurface (PWAT 0.70) and model forecasts have this dry layer \nexpanding vertically with time with forecast PWAT of 0.23 by \n12Z/8AM Friday.\n\nThe upper low over the area is transferring its energy to\ndeveloping surface low pressure off the mid-Atlantic Coast. \nThis is key to the development of a strong low, which will \neventually move up the Atlantic Coast. In response to the \nstrengthening low, flow turns more north/northwesterly tonight \nand any remaining cloud cover will diminish giving way to clear \nskies by early Friday with sunny skies forecast to finish off \nthe work week. \n\nTemperatures overnight and for the next several nights will be\nquite cool with lows in the 40s and potentially into the upper \n30s for the higher mountain elevations. These cool temperatures\nwill remain in place through the weekend, but will begin to \nmoderate with return flow next week. No rain expected for at \nleast the next week.",
